To stop fetching external definitions, such as DTDs, while processing an XML document in Perl using XML::XPath, you can configure the XML::Parser to not use LWP for resolving external entities. You can achieve this by creating an XML::Parser object with the `NoLWP` option set to `1`, and then passing this parser object to XML::XPath. Here’s an example:

```perl
use XML::XPath;
use XML::Parser;

my $p = XML::Parser->new(NoLWP => 1);
my $xp = XML::XPath->new(parser => $p, filename => "your_file.xml");
```

This approach will prevent the parser from attempting to fetch the DTD over HTTP, thus speeding up the processing. Note that you will lose all entities except for numerical ones and the default ones (like `>`, `<`, `&`, `'`, and `"`), as the parser will not handle them anymore [How can I prevent XML::XPath from fetching a DTD while processing an XML file?](303510).

To create a query string from a list of field names in Java, you can use a similar approach to PHP's `http_build_query` function. A typical implementation involves iterating over a `Map` of field names and their corresponding values, encoding them and appending them to a `StringBuffer`. Here's an example implementation:

```java
public String toQueryString(Map<String, String> data) throws UnsupportedEncodingException {
    StringBuffer queryString = new StringBuffer();
    for (Map.Entry<String, String> pair : data.entrySet()) {
        queryString.append(URLEncoder.encode(pair.getKey(), "UTF-8") + "=");
        queryString.append(URLEncoder.encode(pair.getValue(), "UTF-8") + "&");
    }
    if (queryString.length() > 0) {
        queryString.deleteCharAt(queryString.length() - 1); // Remove the last '&'
    }
    return queryString.toString();
}
```

This method encodes each key-value pair and concatenates them into a single query string. If you want a more structured approach, consider using a `QueryStringBuilder` class that handles parameter encoding and string construction more elegantly, as shown in the earlier context [Is there any Java equivalent of PHP's http_build_query function?](Post ID: 636770).
